NAME
       nmap - scan TCP ports

SYNOPSIS
       nmap [-p 1-1024|22,80,443|-] [--timeout ms] <host>

DESCRIPTION
       Tries to open a TCP connection to each port of HOST and reports
       which ones accept. Connections are made without blocking, so a
       wide range finishes quickly.

OPTIONS
       -p SPEC        ports to scan: a range, a list, or - for all
       --timeout MS   how long to wait for each connection

EXAMPLES
       nmap -p 1-1024 10.0.0.1
       nmap -p 22,80,443 example.com

SEE ALSO
       nc(1), ping(1)
